# Suite pack (plan 04-15, D-26): per listing of data/expected/listings.ids, ivs_pack --dump-words
# equals the listing step's own parse (cmake -DDUMP=<id> -P tools/check/listing.cmake) byte for
# byte. pack.trailer-<id> (plan 04-16): the IVSC trailer of a cart listing equals cmake -E sha256sum
# of the container minus its last 32 bytes.
pack.words-boot-stub
pack.words-boot-stub-2
pack.words-diag-cpu-1
pack.trailer-diag-cpu-1
pack.words-ivs-diag-ctrl-psg-1
pack.trailer-ivs-diag-ctrl-psg-1
pack.words-ivs-diag-stic-1
pack.trailer-ivs-diag-stic-1
pack.words-ivs-demo-lamp-tone-1
pack.trailer-ivs-demo-lamp-tone-1
pack.words-ivs-diag-stic-2
pack.trailer-ivs-diag-stic-2
# pack.judge.patched-word (plan 04-24, D-46): self-control of the words comparison; passes only when
# the comparison fails on ivs_pack's dump of the first listing with its first word patched.
pack.judge.patched-word
# pack.c-include.write-error (review IN-08): a failed write of --c-include is the documented
# write error line, a nonzero exit and no output file.
pack.c-include.write-error
# The wrap tool (plan 14-01, D-47, TOOL-07): one case per token pinned in data/expected/flat-refusals.ids,
# minted by a loop over that file, each asserting the refusal (exit 1, one stderr line with the token, nothing
# on stdout, no output file) and its boundary positive (exit 0, one 64-hex line, a container of the exact
# expected size, and the value read back where the pair is about a value).
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-empty: a zero-byte input is refused (a container segment holds at least one word, so
# no container exists for it); one word (2 bytes) is accepted as the smallest legal container, 66 bytes, entry
# 40000001.
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-empty
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-length: 1 byte refused, 2 bytes accepted as one word.
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-length
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-word-range: 0400 refused, 03FF accepted and its container word is 03FF.
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-word-range
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-words: a token pair, not a refuse-to-accept pair. 65,537 words is refused by the
# count rule and 65,536 words by the crossing rule, because IVS_IVSC_MAX_SEGMENT_WORDS is 65,535 and
# $4000 + 65536 = $14000 crosses $10000 first; the case pins the count rule's threshold at 65,536.
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-words
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-base: base 3FFF refused, 4000 accepted.
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-base
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-cross: 49,153 words at 4000 refused, 49,152 accepted with its last word at FFFF
# (the entry reads 4000c000).
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-cross
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-output-tree: the literal spelling, a `..` spelling and a symlink to a directory
# inside the work tree are all refused; a path outside it is accepted.
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-output-tree
# pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-output-exists: an existing file is refused and left byte-identical; a new path is
# accepted.
pack.flatwrap.neg.flatwrap-output-exists
# pack.judge.flatwrap-tokens: the pinned tokens are the literals tools/flatwrap/flatwrap.c can print, once each
# and well-formed, and every one of them was observed by a case above.
pack.judge.flatwrap-tokens
# pack.judge.flatwrap-digest-live: the printed digest is sha256sum of the whole container and the trailer is
# sha256sum of every byte before it; the same input twice gives the same digest and one flipped input byte moves
# both, which is the liveness guard.
pack.judge.flatwrap-digest-live
